  "question": {
    "text": "At present, a firm is manufacturing <math><mn>2</mn> <mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn></math> items. It is estimated that the rate of change of production <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> w.r.t. additional number of workers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math>.&nbsp;If the firm employs <math><mn>2</mn> <mn>5</mn> </math> more workers, then the new level of production of items is",
